166 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 90 0 R
/T (In such an environment, strategic autonomy has evolved beyond a simple doctrine of non-alignment or policy independence into something far more dynamic. It is the means by which states can safeguard their sovereignty and decision-making prerogatives, expand their partnerships and agency, and all the while sidestep the rigidities of bloc politics. Theoretical lenses offer various ways to read this: for the realist it is about the balance of power and survival; liberal institutionalism points to its function within multilateral bodies and issue-based coalitions; constructivists would stress how identity and history inform foreign policy; and from a critical or postcolonial vantage point it is seen as an assertion of political and epistemic autonomy in the face of entrenched hierarchies.)
/E (In such an environment, strategic autonomy has evolved beyond a simple doctrine of non-alignment or policy independence into something far more dynamic. It is the means by which states can safeguard their sovereignty and decision-making prerogatives, expand their partnerships and agency, and all the while sidestep the rigidities of bloc politics. Theoretical lenses offer various ways to read this: for the realist it is about the balance of power and survival; liberal institutionalism points to its function within multilateral bodies and issue-based coalitions; constructivists would stress how identity and history inform foreign policy; and from a critical or postcolonial vantage point it is seen as an assertion of political and epistemic autonomy in the face of entrenched hierarchies.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
