/E (Before colonization of the British, the Kuki-Mizos dwelled in traditional tribal societies and had their own distinct, ancestral religion, which mentioned a mysterious progenitor called Manasia or Manmasi. Through colonization, the community was Christianized. As they came to know the Bible,many were struck by parallels between its stories and commandments and elements of their old preChristian religion. This belief began to spread that Manasiya or Manmasi was the biblical Manasseh, the son of Joseph and that the Kuki-Mizos were descendants from the tribe named after him; one of the ten tribes that vanished after the Assyrian Empire conquered the kingdom of Israel in 722 BCE and exiled much of its population. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
